+# Design: Testing Your Next Chapter
+
+## Direction
+
+An editorial “experiment notebook” built from clean cards, route diagrams, underlines, and evidence stamps. The progression moves from a closed circular thought loop to an open route with three concrete stops.
+
+## Palette and type
+
+- Navy `#0d2437` and deep navy `#0a1e2f`: foundation and authority
+- Blue `#3393d6`: exploration and connection
+- Gold `#eaab2d`: decisions and evidence
+- Paper `#ffffff`, cultured `#f6f6f9`: note cards
+- Proxima Nova with the system fallback from `tokens.yml`
+
+## Layout
+
+Keep content inside 120px frame padding and above the 960px content boundary. A persistent module label sits in the upper left. Large ideas use 72–104px type; supporting copy is never below 40px. Each scene has one dominant graphic and no more than three supporting elements.
+
+## Motion
+
+One paused GSAP timeline controls all motion and is registered as `m5_testing-your-next-chapter`. Each beat enters within 1.2 seconds, holds for reading, and exits in 0.3 seconds. Lines draw left-to-right, cards rise 28px into place, and evidence stamps land with a restrained scale settle. There are no infinite animations.
+
